import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"The type system","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"handl/explanation/type-system.md","filePath":"vendored/handl/explanation/type-system.md"}`),a={name:`handl/explanation/type-system.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="the-type-system" tabindex="-1">The type system <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-type-system" aria-label="Permalink to “The type system”">​</a></h1><p>Handl&#39;s types are <strong>values</strong>, and the checker is a normaliser. There is no separate type syntax layer: <code>Nat</code>, <code>Vec&lt;3, Bool&gt;</code> and <code>Type(0)</code> are ordinary values in the same tagged representation as terms, which is why a type may mention a term and a term may be inspected as a type.</p><h2 id="unification-is-a-judgment" tabindex="-1">Unification is a judgment <a class="header-anchor" href="#unification-is-a-judgment" aria-label="Permalink to “Unification is a judgment”">​</a></h2><p>Structural equality does not decide everything here: index equalities reduce to arithmetic over symbolic atoms, and some of those are genuinely open. <code>unify</code> therefore answers one of three things.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>answer</th><th>meaning</th><th>what happens</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>Proven</code></td><td>equal for every instantiation</td><td>the check proceeds</td></tr><tr><td><code>Disproven</code></td><td>no instantiation makes them equal</td><td>type error; in a <code>match</code> arm the arm is auto-discharged</td></tr><tr><td><code>Unknown</code></td><td>outside the solver&#39;s fragment</td><td>deferred, warned, or left to the caller</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The solver sits behind an <code>IndexSolver</code> seam. The built-in one normalises index atoms to <strong>ring normal form</strong>, so <code>?k + 1 + m</code> and <code>m + ?k + 1</code> are the same polynomial, adds a linear/division/root fragment with non-negativity facts, and reads the constructor index projections each family declares. Unsolved metavariables participate honestly as ring atoms, which is what lets <code>?k + 1 = var{m} + 1</code> solve by same-operator congruence.</p><p>A solver answering <code>Unknown</code> is the design, not a failure: it is how the system stays sound while its decision procedure stays deliberately partial.</p><h2 id="the-surface" tabindex="-1">The surface <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-surface" aria-label="Permalink to “The surface”">​</a></h2><p>Arrows are the only callable shape, and they are values:</p><div class="language-"><button title="Copy code" data-copied="Copied" class="copy"></button><span class="lang"></span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes handl-dark github-light" style="--shiki-dark:#ffffff;--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark-bg:#2a2a2a;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;" tabindex="0" dir="ltr"><code><span class="line"><span>id      : a ~&gt; a</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>compose : (a ~&gt; b) ~&gt; (b ~&gt; c) ~&gt; (a ~&gt; c)</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Implicit binders are written <code>&lt;...&gt;</code> and come in two kinds that differ in what survives to runtime — <strong>indices</strong> are erased (signatures are typecheck-owned metadata), <strong>evidence</strong> is materialised as a real argument:</p><div class="language-"><button title="Copy code" data-copied="Copied" class="copy"></button><span class="lang"></span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes handl-dark github-light" style="--shiki-dark:#ffffff;--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark-bg:#2a2a2a;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;" tabindex="0" dir="ltr"><code><span class="line"><span>append&lt;n, m, a&gt; : Vec&lt;n, a&gt; ~&gt; Vec&lt;m, a&gt; ~&gt; Vec&lt;n + m, a&gt;</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>lookup&lt;a, ev : Eq(a)&gt;</span></span></code></pre></div><p>A family is declared with a <strong>generator record</strong> (ADR-0158): the field&#39;s codomain decides what the field <em>is</em>.</p><div class="language-"><button title="Copy code" data-copied="Copied" class="copy"></button><span class="lang"></span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes handl-dark github-light" style="--shiki-dark:#ffffff;--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark-bg:#2a2a2a;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;" tabindex="0" dir="ltr"><code><span class="line"><span>Nat := { Zero : Nat, Succ : (pred : Nat) ~&gt; Nat }</span></span>
<span class="line"><span></span></span>
<span class="line"><span>Vec&lt;n : Nat, a : Type&gt; := {</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>  VNil  : Vec&lt;0, a&gt;,</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>  VCons : (x : a, xs : Vec&lt;n, a&gt;) ~&gt; Vec&lt;n + 1, a&gt;</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>}</span></span></code></pre></div><p>A field returning the family is a constructor, folded by <code>match</code> or <code>F.rec</code>; a field returning anything else is an effect operation, folded by <code>handle</code>. That is one mechanism with two readings — which is why the same record form declares <code>State := { get : Unit ~&gt; Nat, put : Nat ~&gt; Unit }</code> and <code>IO</code> becomes an internal marker rather than a separate surface.</p><p>The declaration is also the metadata the checker uses for index projection: declaring the <code>Succ</code> shape makes <code>Vec(Succ n)</code> and <code>Vec(n + 1)</code> definitional in both directions.</p><div class="warning custom-block"><p class="custom-block-title">Write the result index</p><p>A constructor whose result index is left implicit parses, but the checker then synthesises a <em>free</em> metavariable index — and <code>VCons(Zero, true, VNil)</code> will check at <code>Vec&lt;5, Bool&gt;</code>. Always state it.</p></div><h2 id="existentials" tabindex="-1">Existentials <a class="header-anchor" href="#existentials" aria-label="Permalink to “Existentials”">​</a></h2><div class="language-"><button title="Copy code" data-copied="Copied" class="copy"></button><span class="lang"></span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes handl-dark github-light" style="--shiki-dark:#ffffff;--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark-bg:#2a2a2a;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;" tabindex="0" dir="ltr"><code><span class="line"><span>one_vec  : Sigma(Nat, m ~&gt; Vec(m, Bool)) = [Succ(Zero), VCons(true, VNil)]</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>one_vec  : exists m : Nat, Vec(m, Bool)  = [Succ(Zero), VCons(true, VNil)]   -- same type</span></span></code></pre></div><p><code>exists</code> is a spelling of <code>Sigma</code>, introduced by a pair literal whose first component binds the second&#39;s family. The destructured witness binds <strong>rigidly</strong> (<code>var{m}</code> in both results and context, internally renamed so it cannot be shadowed) — that rigidity is what lets a computing <code>filter</code> rebuild its own result type:</p><div class="language-"><button title="Copy code" data-copied="Copied" class="copy"></button><span class="lang"></span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes handl-dark github-light" style="--shiki-dark:#ffffff;--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark-bg:#2a2a2a;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;" tabindex="0" dir="ltr"><code><span class="line"><span>filter&lt;n, a&gt; : (a ~&gt; Bool) ~&gt; Vec&lt;n, a&gt; ~&gt; Sigma(Nat, m ~&gt; Vec(m, a))</span></span></code></pre></div><h2 id="coverage" tabindex="-1">Coverage <a class="header-anchor" href="#coverage" aria-label="Permalink to “Coverage”">​</a></h2><p><code>match</code> on an indexed family is checked with <strong>split trees</strong>, not a flat constructor list: each arm refines the scrutinee&#39;s indices and the checker explores the refinements. Two consequences are visible in ordinary code — decided-impossible arms are discharged rather than rejected, and <code>absurd</code> stays legal documentation without being required. A family the solver cannot decide produces a <em>coverage-unknown</em> warning rather than a silent pass.</p><h2 id="dimensions" tabindex="-1">Dimensions <a class="header-anchor" href="#dimensions" aria-label="Permalink to “Dimensions”">​</a></h2><p>Higher cells are one indexed family, checked generically in the dimension:</p><div class="language-"><button title="Copy code" data-copied="Copied" class="copy"></button><span class="lang"></span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes handl-dark github-light" style="--shiki-dark:#ffffff;--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark-bg:#2a2a2a;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;" tabindex="0" dir="ltr"><code><span class="line"><span>A ~[2]~&gt; B      -- a 2-cell: an arrow whose endpoints are arrows</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>&gt;&gt;&gt;[k]          -- composition at dimension k</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>id_k            -- identity cell at dimension k</span></span></code></pre></div><p><code>Hom(n)</code> values normalise as composition trees, with associativity, unit absorption and interchange holding definitionally.</p><h2 id="effects-instances-and-the-top" tabindex="-1">Effects, instances, and the top <a class="header-anchor" href="#effects-instances-and-the-top" aria-label="Permalink to “Effects, instances, and the top”">​</a></h2><p><code>IO&lt;{ ... }&gt;</code> makes effects an index, and <code>handle</code> is a typing operation on that index: covering an op <strong>replaces</strong> its row entry with the handler&#39;s return type, leaving a residual signature. <code>IO&lt;{ puts: Unit, fs }&gt;</code> means &quot;puts is handled and returns <code>Unit</code>; <code>fs</code> is still performed&quot;. Open rows unify today; they have no surface spelling yet.</p><p>Instances are values, not interfaces: <code>instance Eq(Nat) := { eq: ... }</code> registers a dictionary, coherence is enforced when the instance is <em>declared</em> (overlap is rejected, not resolved later), and an <code>ev : Eq(a)</code> binder receives that dictionary at runtime.</p><p><code>type.unknown</code> is the dynamic top: host results are accepted anywhere, and it is deliberately opaque to <code>==</code>, <code>&lt;</code>, <code>+</code> and <code>if</code>. Passable anywhere, computable nowhere until narrowed.</p><h2 id="what-is-not-there-yet" tabindex="-1">What is not there yet <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-is-not-there-yet" aria-label="Permalink to “What is not there yet”">​</a></h2><p>An SMT backend behind <code>IndexSolver</code> (nonlinear and modular index facts stay <code>Unknown</code>), a surface spelling for open effect rows, quotient/higher inductive types (design note only), and full backend parity for self-recursive arrows. The normative sources are ADR-0106 with 0152/0153/0154; the phase-4 spec orders what remains.</p>`,33)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};